WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.320
hey it's professor Dave, let's talk about
redox chemistry.

00:00:09.420 --> 00:00:17.480
an oxidation-reduction reaction or a redox reaction is
one in which electron transfer occurs. take for

00:00:17.490 --> 00:00:22.250
example this single replacement reaction.
watch what happens if we write out the

00:00:22.250 --> 00:00:29.179
net ionic equation. the sulfates cancel
and we see that the only chemistry that

00:00:29.179 --> 00:00:35.880
has occurred is that two electrons are
transferred from iron to copper. iron has

00:00:35.880 --> 00:00:42.440
lost electrons so it has been oxidized.
copper has gained electrons so it has

00:00:42.440 --> 00:00:47.730
been reduced. it may seem confusing to
associate a reduction with a gain of

00:00:47.730 --> 00:00:55.379
electrons so instead associate reduction
with a reducing of charge. copper 2+

00:00:55.379 --> 00:01:01.160
had its charge reduced to zero when it
gained two electrons. more electrons

00:01:01.160 --> 00:01:06.619
means a more negative or lower charge.
the substance that is oxidized is the

00:01:06.619 --> 00:01:11.000
reducing agent because it's the thing
that caused the reduction in the other

00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:16.509
substance. likewise the substance that is
reduced is the oxidizing agent because

00:01:16.509 --> 00:01:22.830
it caused the oxidation in the other
substance. we will use oxidation numbers

00:01:22.830 --> 00:01:27.640
to keep track of electron flow. these are
like hypothetical charge values for each

00:01:27.640 --> 00:01:32.869
atom in a molecule but they are not
actual electrical charges. here are some

00:01:32.869 --> 00:01:38.390
rules for a signing oxidation numbers.
for an element the oxidation number is

00:01:38.390 --> 00:01:44.390
always zero. if it's a monatomic ion the
oxidation number is the same as the

00:01:44.390 --> 00:01:51.079
charge on the ion. oxygen is almost
always -2 except for in peroxides

00:01:51.079 --> 00:01:57.479
so we can usually assume -2. for
a neutral molecule oxidation numbers

00:01:57.479 --> 00:02:03.719
must add up to zero so if the oxygens in
carbon dioxide are each -2 the carbon

00:02:03.719 --> 00:02:09.440
must be +4. for polyatomic ions the
oxidation numbers must add up to the

00:02:09.440 --> 00:02:13.340
charge on the ion and hydrogen is almost
almost

00:02:13.340 --> 00:02:18.700
always +1. using these numbers for
oxygen and hydrogen we can usually

00:02:18.700 --> 00:02:20.730
assign all the other numbers accordingly.

00:02:20.730 --> 00:02:25.180
let's take a look at a reaction, on the
left we have elements so those have

00:02:25.180 --> 00:02:30.330
oxidation numbers of zero. on the right
we know oxygen will be -2 and

00:02:30.330 --> 00:02:36.660
there's three of them so we need iron to
be + 3 for everything to add to zero. this means

00:02:36.660 --> 00:02:42.090
the iron was oxidized since its
oxidation number increased. oxygen was

00:02:42.090 --> 00:02:47.450
the oxidizing agent. oxygen was also
reduced since its oxidation number

00:02:47.450 --> 00:02:53.210
decreased, that makes iron the reducing
agent. let's check comprehension

